      "writtenOn": "2026-01-08T22:00:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Google Maven Storage bucket (https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com) appears to host only two kinds of artifacts:\n\n* the Prolog compiler and runtime\n* the Gitiles servlet and Gitiles blame-cache\n\nSee:\n\n```python\ntools/deps.bzl:PROLOG_REPO \u003d GERRIT\ntools/deps.bzl:GITILES_REPO \u003d GERRIT\n```\n\nIt might be possible (not tested yet) to temporarily extract these artifacts into a dedicated dependency module, for example `google-deps`.\n\nFor instance:\n\n```python\nmaven.install(\n    name \u003d \"google-deps\",\n    repositories \u003d [\n        \"https://gerrit-maven.storage.googleapis.com\",\n    ],\n    ...\n)\n```\n\nand then define a dedicated TOML file for this module:\n\n```python\nmaven.from_toml(\n    name \u003d \"google-deps\",\n    libs_versions_toml \u003d \"//tools:google-deps.toml\",\n)\n```\n\nWith this approach, we could potentially remove the Google Storage bucket from line 58 above and avoid the related warnings.",
